Journey: Broker FNOL <caseId> is refused with <expectedStatus> <expectedError>
Id: fnol-validation
Tags: @api @negative @regression @contract
Risk: 3
Requirements: API-4, FNOL-3
Description: Negative first-notice-of-loss cases from a CSV owned by the business analysts; rows with runFlag N are not run. Every error response is also validated against the OpenAPI contract.

Call API "POST ${API_URL}/v1/claims" with body '{"policyId":"<policyId>","type":"<type>","incidentDate":"<incidentDate>","amountClaimed":<amount>,"description":"<description>"}' with errors allowed as broker and store as refused
Expect ${refused.status} == ${expectedStatus}
Expect response refused "$.error" equals "<expectedError>"
Expect response refused "$.message" contains "<expectedMessage>"
Count the rows of query "SELECT id FROM claims WHERE description = '<description>'" on claims as created
Expect ${created} == 0

Examples: from data "data/fnol-negative.csv" where runFlag = Y
